      "writtenOn": "2015-09-21T14:36:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Perhaps you copied MigrationNotProvided, which is an error that is not raised to the HTTP API. Your new exception class extends the Python built-in Exception, which basically means you\u0027re supressing your IndexError by discarding all information about the actual exception and replacing it with your own. You\u0027ve actually removed all value to the exception, instead of contributing any whatsoever. Your message_format will never, ever be used.\n\nIf you do in fact intend to raise a 500, which is what this is doing, albeit in an unhandled manner, extend UnexpectedError, not Exception.\n\nAlso, what are operators meant to do when they receive this error message? There\u0027s very little clue in the message itself, beyond the keyword \"mapping.\" A more verbose error message would be much appreciated... *especially* if this is going to otherwise raise a generic 500.\n\nIf keystone has been configured incorrectly by the operator, a 500 may indeed be appropriate, but the error message is simply not useful in the context of a 500.",
      "revId": "6caaa91cc2f89d85a086c2afbf8686da76e47cdc",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
